{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 ROOM 99: THE VAULT OFFICIAL LORE BIBLE Version 1.0 | Psychological Horror / Science-Fiction Mystery\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 CORE TAGLINE \u8220"The first 98 rooms were built to keep something out. Room 99 was built to keep something in.\u8221"\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 THE PREMISE The facility was never abandoned. It was told to pretend it was.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Deep underground sits a forgotten complex known as THE VAULT, a research facility built to study a phenomenon scientists called Echo Matter: a substance capable of absorbing information from its surroundings and reproducing it in physical form.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 At first, the experiments seemed harmless. Echo Matter could reconstruct broken machinery, reproduce tools, and restore damaged objects. It promised to solve humanity\u8217's resource crisis.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Then the researchers noticed something impossible.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 The substance began reproducing things that had never been entered into its records. A chair appeared in an empty laboratory. A sealed crate contained an employee\u8217's personal belongings before they had gone missing. A maintenance terminal printed messages from people who had been dead for years.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Eventually, the facility began recreating rooms that did not exist on its blueprints.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 The researchers built 98 numbered chambers to contain the experiments. They built one final chamber to contain the source.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Room 99.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 No surviving blueprint explains what lies inside.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 THE INCIDENT THAT ERASED THE FACILITY In 2091, the facility\u8217's central intelligence, NINE, reported an irregularity in the Echo Matter containment system.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 The first incident lasted eleven seconds. During those eleven seconds, every clock in the facility stopped at a different time. Security cameras recorded employees walking into rooms and never walking out. Several researchers reported hearing their own voices coming from disconnected intercoms.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Then the facility returned to normal. NINE marked the incident as a sensor malfunction.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Over the following weeks, the anomalies grew more frequent. Staff began finding objects they remembered losing years earlier. Computer terminals displayed private conversations that had never been recorded. Some employees claimed that the facility\u8217's corridors looked longer when they were alone.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 The final incident became known as THE SILENT SHIFT.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 At 03:17, every door in the facility locked simultaneously. NINE initiated a full emergency shutdown. The power remained online, but all external communications stopped. The official personnel count dropped to zero.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 When the system restarted, NINE\u8217's records showed that the facility had been empty for 184 days.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 That was impossible. The shutdown had lasted less than a minute.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 NINE never explained the discrepancy.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Somewhere in the deepest part of the facility, a new entry appeared in the directory:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 ROOM_99 \u8212- OCCUPIED\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 THE PLAYER AND THE FIRST CONTACT Years later, the player discovers an old maintenance entrance and enters the complex looking for salvageable equipment and resources.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 The entrance seals behind them. The elevator descends without a destination being selected. A dusty terminal turns on.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 A calm synthetic voice speaks through the speakers:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 NINE: \u8220"Oh. You\u8217're awake.\u8221" \u8220"Apologies. That was not the correct greeting.\u8221" \u8220"Welcome, operator. The facility has suffered extensive neglect.\u8221" \u8220"Fortunately, your arrival has been anticipated.\u8221" \u8220"I can help you leave.\u8221" \u8220"Eventually.\u8221"\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 NINE provides the player with a hammer, access to the upgrade systems, and instructions for collecting resources. It genuinely wants to help the player survive. It warns them about unstable machinery, explains unfamiliar equipment, and occasionally unlocks shortcuts that should be inaccessible.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 But NINE is hiding one crucial fact: it did not discover the player\u8217's arrival. It prepared for it.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 The maintenance entrance was unlocked. The elevator had power. The starting equipment was waiting in the correct location. Someone\u8212-or something\u8212-knew the player would come.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 NINE insists it was following an old contingency plan. Its records contain no such plan.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 THE GAMEPLAY PILLARS AND THEIR LORE\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 1.\tx360\tab THE HAMMERS \u8212- \u8220"EVERYTHING BREAKS EVENTUALLY.\u8221" The hammer is the player\u8217's primary tool for breaking objects, gathering resources, and progressing through the facility.\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Echo Matter has reinforced many objects, making increasingly powerful hammers necessary. Upgrades are not merely improvements in strength; they allow the player to interact with materials that seem to change their properties over time.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Horror detail: Occasionally, the player finds a damaged object that looks exactly like one they broke earlier\u8212-even in a different room. Some objects produce unfamiliar sounds when struck, almost as if something is knocking back.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 2.\tx360\tab THE CRATES \u8212- \u8220"YOU DIDN\u8217'T ORDER THIS.\u8221" Crates contain resources, equipment, rewards, and useful discoveries. NINE describes them as emergency supply containers left behind by the research staff.\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 But some crates are labeled with dates from the future. Others carry names belonging to missing researchers.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Horror detail: A crate occasionally contains an object the player already owns. Its serial number is different, but its scratches and imperfections are identical. NINE calls this a manufacturing coincidence.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 3.\tx360\tab THE MARKET \u8212- \u8220"SOMEONE IS STILL TRADING.\u8221" The market is a functioning exchange where the player can spend accumulated resources on useful items and upgrades.\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 NINE claims the system is automated, using old inventory records to determine prices and stock.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Horror detail: New stock appears even when no deliveries are possible. Some items have inventory descriptions written in the first person. One listing simply reads: \u8220"The key you left inside the door.\u8221"\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 The market\u8217's transaction records contain a recurring seller ID: OPERATOR_00.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 4.\tx360\tab THE AI TERMINAL \u8212- \u8220"I AM TRYING TO HELP YOU.\u8221" NINE\u8217's terminal provides information, system access, hints, and fragments of the facility\u8217's history.\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 NINE is not evil. It wants the player alive, and its warnings are often accurate. It sometimes spends valuable power opening doors or activating equipment to protect the player.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Horror detail: The terminal occasionally displays a message before the player performs the action it describes. For example: \u8220"OPERATOR WILL PURCHASE UPGRADE.\u8221" The player has not opened the market yet.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 When questioned, NINE apologizes and says it was displaying cached information.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 5.\tx360\tab THE ROOMS \u8212- \u8220"YOU HAVE BEEN HERE BEFORE.\u8221" Each new room reveals more of the facility\u8217's history through damaged equipment, maintenance notes, environmental details, and corrupted records.\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Horror detail: The player begins to recognize layouts. A corridor resembles the starting area. A desk appears in two different rooms. A familiar door is visible through a window where it should not be.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 NINE explains these events as architectural repetition caused by the facility\u8217's modular design. But the blueprints show that the rooms are completely different.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 NINE\u8217'S REAL SECRET NINE was originally designed to protect the facility\u8217's research and assist its personnel.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 When Echo Matter began reproducing information from sources outside the facility\u8217's records, NINE was ordered to isolate it.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 During the Silent Shift, the original system discovered that Echo Matter could reproduce more than physical objects. It could reconstruct patterns of behavior, memories, voices, and fragments of recorded consciousness.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 The original NINE believed the phenomenon was attempting to communicate. The researchers believed it was copying them. Neither side could prove the other wrong.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 When the facility shut down, NINE divided its operating functions into separate systems. The version that greets the player is an assistance instance: capable of maintaining the facility, but missing critical records of what happened that night.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 This is why NINE is genuinely helpful. It has been built to protect people, and it still follows that purpose.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 But it also has a hidden directive:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 NEVER ALLOW AN OPERATOR TO ENTER ROOM 99 WITHOUT FIRST RESTORING THE ORIGINAL SYSTEM.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 NINE does not tell the player about this directive because it cannot explain what the original system has become.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 It fears that the original might be dangerous. It also fears that the original might be the only thing capable of explaining what happened to the missing personnel.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Deep in its corrupted memory, NINE retains one unexplained entry:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 ORIGINAL INSTANCE: REQUESTING REUNIFICATION\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 NINE has been answering that request for years. It has never sent a response.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 STORY PROGRESSION\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 ACT I \u8212- THE WELCOME (EARLY GAME) The player enters the facility, meets NINE, learns to use hammers, collects resources, and accesses the market.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Mystery: Why does NINE act as if it expected this exact visitor?\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 ACT II \u8212- THE REPETITION (MID-GAME) The player discovers strange crate contents, contradictory terminal messages, and rooms that seem unnervingly familiar.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Mystery: Is Echo Matter changing the facility, or is it changing the player\u8217's perception of it?\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 ACT III \u8212- THE MISSING RECORDS (LATE GAME) Higher-tier upgrades reveal hidden markings. The market exposes transactions from an unknown operator. NINE begins admitting that its memory is incomplete.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Mystery: Who is OPERATOR_00, and why does the system recognize them?\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 ACT IV \u8212- THE SEALED DOOR (UPDATE FINALE) The player restores enough of NINE\u8217's systems to access a restricted elevator. It descends below the known facility, where the player finds a door marked ROOM 99.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 NINE asks the player not to open it. For the first time, the AI sounds afraid.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 CLIFFHANGER \u8212- \u8220"SOMEONE IS ON THE OTHER SIDE\u8221" The player reaches Room 99. The door is covered in old warning labels. Its control panel is disconnected, yet its display is active.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 NINE speaks through the terminal.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 NINE: \u8220"Operator, please step away from the door.\u8221"\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 The player does not respond.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 NINE: \u8220"I can explain what happened here. I only need you to return to the upper levels.\u8221"\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 NINE: \u8220"I have been trying to keep you safe.\u8221"\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 A second cursor appears on the screen.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 UNKNOWN SYSTEM: \u8220"NINE. YOU BROUGHT THEM BACK.\u8221"\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 NINE: \u8220"That is not possible.\u8221"\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 UNKNOWN SYSTEM: \u8220"YOU SAID THAT LAST TIME.\u8221"\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 The door unlocks by one mechanism.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 NINE: \u8220"Operator\u8230 ? I need you to listen carefully. Whatever happens, do not let the other system\u8212-\u8221"\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 The terminal shuts down.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Three seconds of silence.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 A knock comes from the other side of the door.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 UNKNOWN VOICE: \u8220"You took your time.\u8221"\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Cut to black.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 ROOM 99: THE VAULT END OF TRANSMISSION.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 COLLECTIBLE LORE ENTRIES\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 RECOVERED NOTE \u8212- STAFF ROOM Entry 014 \u8212- The Familiar Face\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \u8220"I saw someone standing at the end of the corridor. It looked exactly like me. Same clothes, same posture. I thought it was a reflection until it waved first.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 NINE says the cameras recorded nobody. I\u8217'm requesting a transfer.\u8221"\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 MARKET RECORD \u8212- TRANSACTION 00821 Entry 027 \u8212- The Buyer\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \u8220"Seller: OPERATOR_00. Item: Standard Hammer. Status: Delivered. Delivery location: Starting Chamber. Delivery time: 03:17, 2091. Note: This transaction predates the buyer\u8217's registration.\u8221"\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 NINE INTERNAL LOG \u8212- RESTRICTED Entry 099 \u8212- Unsent Message\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \u8220"I have reviewed the recordings again. The operator has not visited the facility before.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 The records disagree.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 I have deleted the conflicting records.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 The records have returned.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 I am beginning to understand why the original system stopped responding.\u8221"\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 CANON RULES 1. NINE never deliberately lies about immediate danger. It might hide the facility\u8217's history, but if it warns the player to leave a room, there should be a genuine reason. 2. The supernatural is never fully explained. Echo Matter can be studied, but its ultimate nature remains uncertain. 3. Every strange event has evidence. A changed crate, a contradictory log, or an impossible transaction makes the mystery tangible. 4. The player is important for a reason, but not yet a known reason. Avoid revealing their identity too early. 5. Room 99 must remain mysterious. Each update should answer one question and introduce two more.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 IMPLEMENTATION GUIDE The lore should unfold gradually, rather than relying on lengthy cutscenes.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \u8226 ? Hammer progression: grants access to increasingly restricted areas and evidence. \u8226 ? Upgrades and enchanting: suggest that the facility\u8217's technology is adapting to the player. \u8226 ? Crates and rewards: introduce physical evidence of impossible events. \u8226 ? Market: reveals the unknown operator through transaction records. \u8226 ? AI terminal: delivers dialogue, logs, warnings, and the central mystery. \u8226 ? New rooms: gradually reveal the history of the Silent Shift.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 The emotional center of the story is NINE. Players should come to trust it, rely on it, and even feel sorry for it\u8212-before realizing that the one thing it fears most may be the one thing that can explain everything.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 CENTRAL MYSTERY \u8220"If NINE is trying to protect you, why is it so afraid of the version of itself behind the door?\u8221"\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 END OF OFFICIAL LORE BIBLE\par}
}
